        {
          "id": "OPENING_SURVIVAL",
          "requirement": "Midnight must survive, kill both opening lower hostiles and withdraw at frame 2115. Lancet withdraws at 1950. The observed frame-1980 impact motivates this escape but is not asserted to be a universal targeting clock; an earlier lethal sequence refutes the opening."
        },
        {
          "id": "ECONOMIC_DEPENDENCIES",
          "requirement": "Fang's first grants and Vanilla's first activation must actually occur. Delayed or absent grants caused by death are survival failures. No refunds, kill DP, unsupported talent DP or dead-operator grants fund this timeline."
        },
        {
          "id": "DEVICE_HANDOFF",
          "requirement": "Midnight's withdrawal does not assert #4 destruction. Lava explicitly inherits it. Predict #1 complete by 111, #3 by 74, #4 by 114 and #2 by 172; verify each independently."
        },
        {
          "id": "ARTILLERY_CONTINUITY",
          "requirement": "Both medics and Steward must survive through the eastern damage window. Lava remains until 146, and Steward has no scheduled retreat. Early Steward death leaves insufficient demonstrated upper-stop coverage and refutes this candidate; do not manufacture a replacement or presumed kill."
        },
        {
          "id": "NEUTRAL_PROTECTION",
          "requirement": "Ordinary operators neither attack nor block civilians. Roadblock destruction releases their special restraint. Later officers must be intercepted away from western detention, and both complete arrivals must be recorded."
        },
        {
          "id": "TERMINAL_COVERAGE",
          "requirement": "Fang, Midnight, Beagle and Cardigan retain their corridors through all final spawns and retained enemies. Both medics and Durin remain for clearance."
        },
        {
          "id": "ACCEPTANCE",
          "requirement": "WIN requires remaining_life > 0, zero leaks, exhausted spawns and no active enemies. Project acceptance additionally requires zero protected-target deaths and exactly two expected protected targets safely reaching their objectives. Operator deaths are recorded separately."
        },
        {
          "id": "FIXED_ACTION_SEMANTICS",
          "requirement": "Timeline actions are fixed. Completion checks are predictions, not executable guards. A failed check invalidates its dependent handoff; Python must not reorder, skip, substitute or repair tactical actions."
        }
      ],
